   "evidence": "Mathlib has no lemma for this combination: `grep -n 'relIndex_map' mathlib/Mathlib/GroupTheory/Index.lean` yields only `relIndex_map_map_of_injective` (:93) and `relIndex_map_map` (:98); `index_map` (:319) and `index_map_dvd` (:324, needs surjectivity) do not give the relIndex form without cancelling a possibly-zero `f.range.index`. The two in-repo clones are TauCeti/GroupTheory/Index/NSmul.lean:105 and TauCeti/GroupTheory/Index/Basic.lean:173-176.",
   "file": "TauCeti/FieldTheory/Galois/AbsoluteGaloisGroup/Cyclotomic/Index.lean",
   "fix": "Add the general lemma to TauCeti/GroupTheory/Index/Basic.lean, e.g. `theorem Subgroup.relIndex_map_range (f : G \u2192* G') (H : Subgroup G) : (H.map f).relIndex f.range = (H \u2294 f.ker).index := by rw [\u2190 Subgroup.map_top f, Subgroup.relIndex_map_map, top_sup_eq, Subgroup.relIndex_top_right]` (optionally the corollary `(H.map f).relIndex f.range \u2223 H.index := index_dvd_of_le le_sup_left`), then prove `relIndex_range_localCyclotomicCharacter_dvd_finrank` as `rw [range_localCyclotomicCharacter_eq_map p K L \u03c3, Subgroup.relIndex_map_range, \u2190 index_range_absoluteGaloisGroupExtend K L \u03c3]; exact Subgroup.index_dvd_of_le le_sup_left`, and replace the body of the private NSmul lemma with the same shared lemma.",
   "issue": "Lines 60-66 re-derive the purely group-theoretic identity `(U.map f).relIndex f.range = (U \u2294 f.ker).index` (then `index_dvd_of_le le_sup_left`) from `relIndex_map_map`/`map_top`/`top_sup_eq`/`relIndex_top_right`. The same derivation already appears in TauCeti twice: `Subgroup.relIndex_range_comp_subtype` in TauCeti/GroupTheory/Index/NSmul.lean:97-105 (`rw [hU, MonoidHom.range_eq_map \u03c6G, relIndex_map_map, top_sup_eq, relIndex_top_right, sup_comm]`, private and specialized to `powMonoidHom`, hence unusable here) and the finiteness shadow `MonoidHom.finiteIndex_range_comp` in TauCeti/GroupTheory/Index/Basic.lean:170-177 (`Subgroup.index_map` + `finiteIndex_of_le (le_sup_left : \u03c6\u2081.range \u2264 \u03c6\u2081.range \u2294 \u03c6\u2082.ker)`). Nothing about cyclotomic characters is used in this step.",
